  ($tfq$q-tf004-84$tfq$, $tfq$terraform-associate-004$tfq$, $tfq$Medium$tfq$, $tfq$single$tfq$, $tfq$A backend reports that the state is locked by another active operation. What is the safest first response?$tfq$, $tfq$Confirm whether the other operation is still running before taking further action$tfq$, $tfq$Delete the state file so Terraform creates an unlocked replacement$tfq$, $tfq$Run force-unlock immediately without checking the lock owner$tfq$, $tfq$Change the resource names so the current operation uses a different lock$tfq$, NULL, NULL, 0, ARRAY[0]::INTEGER[], $tfq$A lock normally indicates another state-changing operation. The team should first identify and allow the active operation to finish; forcing a lock can permit concurrent writes and state corruption.$tfq$, $tfq$tf004-state$tfq$),
