  ($tfq$q-tf004-89$tfq$, $tfq$terraform-associate-004$tfq$, $tfq$Hard$tfq$, $tfq$multiple$tfq$, $tfq$Which two statements describe safe use of terraform force-unlock? Select two.$tfq$, $tfq$Use the lock ID reported by the failed locking operation$tfq$, $tfq$Confirm that no active operation still owns the lock$tfq$, $tfq$Use it routinely before every automated terraform plan$tfq$, $tfq$Expect it to modify remote infrastructure immediately$tfq$, $tfq$Use it to replace a lost state file with configuration defaults$tfq$, NULL, 0, ARRAY[0, 1]::INTEGER[], $tfq$force-unlock requires the specific lock ID and should be used only after verifying that the lock is stale. It removes a state lock; it does not rebuild state or directly change infrastructure.$tfq$, $tfq$tf004-state$tfq$),
