  ($tfq$q-tf004-93$tfq$, $tfq$terraform-associate-004$tfq$, $tfq$Hard$tfq$, $tfq$single$tfq$, $tfq$A configuration contains an import block with to = aws_s3_bucket.logs and id = "existing-logs". When does Terraform perform the import?$tfq$, $tfq$As part of applying a plan that includes the import action$tfq$, $tfq$Immediately when the configuration file is saved to disk$tfq$, $tfq$Only after the import block is removed from configuration$tfq$, $tfq$During terraform fmt before provider initialization occurs$tfq$, NULL, NULL, 0, ARRAY[0]::INTEGER[], $tfq$Import blocks make import actions plannable and reviewable. Terraform performs the import during apply after the plan is approved, rather than when files are saved or formatted.$tfq$, $tfq$tf004-maintenance$tfq$),
  ($tfq$q-tf004-94$tfq$, $tfq$terraform-associate-004$tfq$, $tfq$Hard$tfq$, $tfq$single$tfq$, $tfq$What is the effect of terraform state rm aws_s3_bucket.archive when the remote bucket still exists?$tfq$, $tfq$Terraform forgets the state binding without deleting the remote bucket$tfq$, $tfq$Terraform deletes the bucket but retains its address in state$tfq$, $tfq$Terraform imports the bucket into a new automatically chosen address$tfq$, $tfq$Terraform encrypts the bucket record and hides it from state list$tfq$, NULL, NULL, 0, ARRAY[0]::INTEGER[], $tfq$terraform state rm removes the binding from state and does not destroy the remote object. If the resource block remains, a later plan may propose creating another object.$tfq$, $tfq$tf004-maintenance$tfq$),
